        "eyebrow": "Virtual staging near you",
        "heading": "Virtual Staging California",
        "lede": "Virtual staging is the digital alternative to physical staging: a designer furnishes photos of empty or cleared rooms with realistic 3D furniture and decor, so buyers see a finished home online without any furniture being delivered. From San Francisco flats to San Diego ranch homes, Bella's designers stage California listings in 24 to 48 hours, from {price:virtual-staging} a photo — with furnishing matched to each metro's buyer.",
        "cta_label": "Stage my listing — from {price:virtual-staging}",
        "cta_link": "/products/virtual-staging",
        "alt_label": "Browse the lookbook",
        "alt_link": "/pages/lookbook",
        "city": "California",
        "market_heading": "Why virtual staging matters across California",
        "market_text": "<p>California is not one market — a Noe Valley Victorian, a Sacramento new build and an Orange County family home attract different buyers with different taste. What they share is price point: with the median California home among the most expensive in the nation, buyers expect listing photos that look like the money being asked.</p><p>Physical staging costs scale with those prices — often thousands per month in coastal metros. Virtual staging delivers the same first impression once, for {price:virtual-staging} a photo, which is why California agents were among our first and remain our largest client base.</p><p>The state also has the clearest disclosure expectations in the country, which is a good thing for agents who want to use staged photos without second-guessing. AB 723 set the standard, and our California work is built to it — disclosure guidance ships with the order rather than being something you assemble afterward.</p><p>It matters because the listing photos do the first showing: 97% of buyers use the internet in their home search, according to the National Association of Realtors. A virtually staged image of an empty room tells a buyer where the sofa goes, how big the primary bedroom really is and what the space could feel like.</p>",
        "local_heading": "Virtual staging services for every California metro",
        "local_text": "<p>Our designers stage daily for the Bay Area, Los Angeles, San Diego, Sacramento and the Central Valley, matching furniture and palette to each region's buyer. Images are MLS-ready in 24 to 48 hours, disclosed as virtually staged, with unlimited revisions free for two weeks.</p><p>Because we work across every major California board, an agent listing in two metros gets one consistent look rather than two different vendors' idea of what a staged room should be.</p><p>Files are sized for the MLS you list on — CRMLS, SDMLS or The MLS (CLAW) among them — and ship with AB 723 disclosure guidance and full usage rights. Volume discounts apply automatically — 5% at 3+ photos, 10% at 6+, 15% at 11+ and 20% at 21+.</p>",
        "hoods_label": "Where we stage most",
        "hoods": "San Francisco, Oakland, San Jose, Sacramento, Los Angeles, Orange County, San Diego, Central Valley, Palm Springs"
      }
    },
