    "faq": {
      "type": "bella-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "q1": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What does AB 723 actually require of me?",
            "answer": "Two things for any digitally altered listing image: a reasonably conspicuous statement on or next to the image saying it has been altered, and access to the original, unaltered image — included in the posting or through a link or QR code. We build every California order to that standard and send you the disclosure wording. Your broker or MLS is the final word on placement."
          }
        },
        "q2": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "I list in both the Bay Area and Southern California. Same team?",
            "answer": "Same studio, different furnishing. The palette and furniture that sell a Noe Valley Victorian aren't what sell an Orange County family home, so we stage to the metro — but you get one consistent standard of finish across both."
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How does the cost compare to physical staging here?",
            "answer": "It's the sharpest contrast in the country. Physical staging in coastal California metros routinely runs into the thousands per month; virtual staging is {price:virtual-staging} a photo, once, with no rental period to extend if the listing sits."
          }
        },
        "q4": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do you handle new construction with nothing built yet?",
            "answer": "Yes, though that's 3D rendering rather than staging — we build the interior from plans instead of photos. Common for California developers marketing pre-sale inventory."
          }
        },
        "q5": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How much does virtual staging cost?",
            "answer": "Prices vary by provider and by whether a person or an AI app does the work. Bella's designer-made virtual staging is {price:virtual-staging} per photo, with volume discounts of 5% at 3+ photos, 10% at 6+, 15% at 11+ and 20% at 21+. Furniture removal for occupied rooms, unlimited revisions for two weeks and full usage rights are included — no subscription, no minimum."
          }
        },
        "q6": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is virtual staging legal in California?",
            "answer": "Yes, as long as it isn't misleading. Under AB 723 (California Business and Professions Code §10140.8), a digitally altered listing image needs a conspicuous statement on or next to it saying it was altered, plus access to the original, unaltered image — posted alongside it or through a link or QR code. The requirement sits in the state's Real Estate Law, where a violation is a crime, so it's worth getting right. Add furniture and decor only; don't hide defects or change permanent features. Every Bella order includes disclosure guidance, and your broker or MLS has the final say on placement."
          }
        },
        "q7": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is virtual staging worth it?",
            "answer": "For most vacant or dated listings, yes. Staging can't guarantee a sale, but 97% of buyers use the internet in their home search, according to the National Association of Realtors, so the photos decide which homes get a showing. NAR's research on home staging also finds that staging makes it easier for buyers to visualize a property as their future home. At California price points, staged listing photos give buyers the full picture of an empty home for a one-time cost per image instead of monthly furniture rental."
          }
        },
        "q8": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can you show a room in more than one style, or a home that isn't built yet?",
            "answer": "Yes. Because the furniture is digital, a room can be staged in more than one Look Book style, which makes it easy to test which look suits the buyer. For dated rooms, virtual renovation (from {price:virtual-renovation-service}) shows new floors, walls and finishes; for homes that aren't built yet, 3D rendering (from {price:3d-rendering}) creates photorealistic images from plans."
          }
        },
        "q9": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How can I virtually stage my home for free?",
            "answer": "Free AI apps and DIY software can drop furniture into a photo, but the results often distort scale and finishes, and a misleading image creates disclosure problems. New clients can claim a $40 voucher on Bella's sign-up page to try designer-made staging, subject to Bella's approval."
          }
        },
        "q10": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is virtual staging good for luxury listings?",
            "answer": "Yes, if it's realistic. Luxury buyers compare the photos with the real room at the showing, so furniture has to be true to scale and finishes. That's why Bella has real interior designers compose every room rather than an AI app."
          }
        }
      },
